{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Zarach</b> — Troubles are like darkness, as in \"the people walking in darkness,\" and salvation like light, hence \"though I sit in darkness, YHWH is light to me.\" And so when troubles come upon the world, light shines for the upright, and it is HaShem, for He is gracious and compassionate and righteous. Or, light may be drawn after His people, as though it were gracious light."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 112, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:28.483699721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}